// REJECTS: Unexpected token '{'
//
// A Mapping body is delimited by PARENTHESES; every other element type uses braces. The
// MappingLexerGrammar comment calls this a historical quirk and it is the reason Mapping
// needs an island grammar at all.
//
// Pinned because it is the single most plausible thing for a rewrite to normalise away out
// of tidiness, and doing so would accept models legend-engine rejects.
###Mapping
Mapping fixture::neg::Braces
{
   fixture::neg::Person: Relational
   {
      firstName: [fixture::neg::Db]T.FIRST_NAME
   }
}
